    "poem": "\u2022 Tide\n  Hushed glass\n  Every empty umbra\n  Each entrance remembers threshold,\n  Inside cold circuits measure mercury\n  Low currents braid a patient spiral\n  Every hidden hinge keeps bright black quartz\n  Eight patient lanterns lean beyond the tarnished velvet\n  Night gathers its slow map around one waiting harbor\n  Light threads through narrow seams and names the buried cipher\n  Across the floor a single moth keeps circling one iron lantern\n  Under sealed stone the old lock holds 0b1234567890 beyond every blue zero.\n\n"
