    "poem": "\u2022 Time  \n  hangs heavy  \n  each breath slows  \n  echoes fold inward softly  \n  inside the dark 8721b4bd042a waits  \n  low lamps lean along the wall  \n  even silence learns to fear the dust  \n  every shadow keeps a patient count of cold  \n  no key no hymn no memory unlocks this thin  \n  long after midnight something whispers through the stones so bright  \n  and still the door remains, unopened holding its hush of rain  \n  under all this weight the chamber keeps one name it never speaks."
