    "poem": "1. The chamber, dark and still,\n2. Echoes of silence fill.\n3. Lights flicker, ghostly trace,\n4. Whispering tales in the space.\n5. Silent sentinel, old and gray,\n6. Watches, unseen, in the fray.\n7. Shadows dance on the wall,\n8. Tales of the past, they enthrall.\n9. A single, lone candle gleams,\n10. In the chamber's depth, it seems.\n11. Hexadecimal seal, 87,\n12. A final word, a silent \"the\"."
